WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.880
Polio vaccine fell from dollars a dose to pennies once the virus left monkey kidneys for steel tanks. This is First Principles Daily, Episode 77. In 1955, a dose of Jonas Sox inactivated polio vaccine, or IPV, began with a monkey. Kidneys were harvested, cells were spread into glass bottles, and polio virus grew on that living lawn before formaldehyde killed it. Manufacturers enlarged a laboratory ritual with more

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:45.880
animals, and more bottles, and the finished shot lived in dollar territory. The immunizing object inside is a few micrograms of protein in half a milliliter of buffer. Those atoms never changed. The dramatic drop only makes sense once you see the

00:00:46.090 --> 00:01:07.270
analogical factory they copied first. The default was not stubbornness, it was the laboratory, copied at factory scale. In 1949, John Ender's Thomas Weller and Frederick Robbins showed that polio virus would grow in non-neural tissue culture. That work won the 1954 Nobel Prize, and made a killed vaccine thinkable.

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:27.850
Jonas Sox took that method as the production template. Primary monkey kidney cells, serum containing medium, glass bottles, then formaldehyde. When the 1954 Francis Field trial succeeded, and the United States licensed the vaccine in April 1955, the manufacturers who rushed in did the analogical thing.

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:53.370
Park Davis, Eli Lilly, Cutter Laboratories, Wyeth, and Pittman Moore ordered more recess monkeys, mostly from India, trypsonized more kidneys and filled more roller bottles. Capacity meant animals and bottles, because that is what the inventors bench used. Each monkey gave two kidneys and a finite sheet of cells that could not be passaged indefinitely, so output rose only by slaughtering more primates.

00:01:53.370 --> 00:02:08.130
Contemination was a recurring tax. The later finding that some early lots carried simian virus 40, or SV 40, a virus native to recess kidney is the most famous receipt. Inactivation followed Sox recipe.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:19.290
Formalin at a high delusion held warm for many days, treated as a protocol to copy rather than a kinetic window to map. Safety testing itself consumed still more monkeys.

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:28.970
Exact factory cost per 1955 dose is not a clean public figure. The March of Dimes and the Federal Crash program blurred the invoices.

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:36.790
The constraint people actually fought over was the monkey supply, which is how you know the field had accepted a bottleneck as natural.

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:46.470
The cutter incident that same spring, in which some lots left the plant still infectious, paralyzed children and froze the analogical process in place.

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:59.710
Testing got heavier, cycle time got longer, and cost did not fall. Then Albert Sabin's live oral vaccine arrived in the early 1960s, cheap to grow and cheap to drip onto a sugar cube.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:08.570
Inactivated polio vaccine spent decades typed as the expensive injectable, inherently so, because that is how it had always been made.

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:20.230
First principles ignores the monkey and starts with the dose itself. A standard inactivated dose is half a milliliter of buffered liquid containing three serotypes of killed polio virus.

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:32.010
Those serotypes are specified in deantigen units, commonly 48 and 32 for types 1, 2 and 3, because immunity to one type does not cover the others.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:40.930
The protein mass of that antigen is in the microgram range. The rest is water, a pinch of salts, and traces of the inactivation chemistry.

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:47.530
Wave the magic wand and arrange those atoms for free, and the bill for the liquid is a fraction of a scent.

00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:55.310
Bulk amino acids and commodity phosphate sell by the kilogram, and a few micrograms is a vanishing slice of a kilogram.

00:03:55.310 --> 00:04:02.210
Add the real hardware of a dose, a type 1 glass vial, a butyl stopper, and aluminum seal.

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:13.450
A rough magic wand estimate for all the stuff still lands well under a dollar, often in the tens of cents, especially if a multi-dose vial spreads the glass across 5 or 10 shots.

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:21.750
That is the floor. The old process sat many times above it. We do not have an audited 1950s cost of goods,

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:25.730
so treat this as visible arithmetic rather than a measured index.

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:36.110
Put a finished dose in dollar territory over 30 cents of vial and liquid, which is already generous to the bottle and monkey era, and you get a ratio around 10.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:46.650
Put 10 cents under it, and the ratio is 20 to 30. That range is the idiot index as a thinking tool, and it says the dollars were never in the virion.

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:57.350
The first break was the sell. Viro, a continuous line from African green monkey kidney, was established in 1962 by Yasumura and Kawakita.

00:04:58.210 --> 00:05:05.930
Unlike primary kidney cells, it can be banked, characterized once for adventitious agents, and expanded to the volume of the tank.

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:10.010
That single substitution deletes the monkey from routine production.

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:19.650
No more per batch slaughter, no more wild caught recess lottery, no more importing a new primary culture's worth of unknown viruses every week.

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:26.990
The trade-off that had to be won was residual host cell DNA and a historical worry about tumor originicity.

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:33.810
Regulators answered with purification and a tight DNA per dose limit, not by returning to the animal.

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:47.170
The second break was surface area. Polio viruses preferred cells are anchorage dependent. They want a wall, not a free floating life, which is why 1955 production looked like a glassware shop.

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:52.710
Bottles give you wall in proportion to the number of vessels you can wash, seed, and stack.

00:05:53.710 --> 00:06:03.430
AL van Weisel at the Netherlands RIVM in the 1970s put the wall on DEAE Dextran microcarrier beads and stirred them in a tank.

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:11.430
A few liters of broth carry the growth surface of a room full of roller bottles. One controlled bioreactor replaces that room.

00:06:12.190 --> 00:06:19.270
Labor collapses, contamination opportunities collapse, and pH and oxygen become instrument loops instead of hope.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:30.070
The engineering bill for that move was sheer, bead settling, and getting cells on and off the carriers. Problems of mixing and trips in, not of biology as destiny.

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:40.670
The third break was the medium. Feetal bovine serum is costly, variable, and a virus risk, and it dumps albumin into the harvest that you must later strip.

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:46.010
Serum-free formulations at scale cut that line item and make downstream cleaner.

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:50.830
The fourth break was treating inactivation as kinetics rather than liturgy.

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:56.210
Formaldehyde cross-linking of a non-enveloped pecorna virus is a process window.

00:06:56.950 --> 00:07:04.690
Too little and you ship live virus. Too much and native deantigen denatures into sea antigen, and the shot goes impotent.

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:10.690
Filtering out aggregates before the formal instep, clumps can shield virions in their cores.

00:07:10.690 --> 00:07:17.230
And locking temperature, concentration, and time turned a copied recipe into a mapped kill curve.

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:21.050
That is the only way a kill step gets both safe and cheap.

00:07:21.890 --> 00:07:23.890
The fifth break was downstream recovery.

00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:31.450
Tengential flow filtration and chromatography meet DNA and protein specs without pouring antigen down the drain.

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:40.430
If you keep 30% of the deantigen instead of 80, you just paid it for nearly three times the upstream tank volume for the same release doses.

00:07:41.150 --> 00:07:49.230
Institute Meru in France, among others, put these moves together in the 1980s into a true industrial Viral Cell IPV process.

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:52.250
Not a bigger monkey farm, a different machine.

00:07:53.050 --> 00:07:58.950
What that machine delivered is a vaccine whose manufacturing cost could finally approach the cheapness of its atoms.

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:02.370
Even if the price a ministry pays is not the same number.

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:13.330
Public tender prices from the United Nations Children's Fund, UNICEF, for standalone IPV in the 2010s, commonly sat in the low single-digit dollars per dose.

00:08:14.030 --> 00:08:16.970
Later competition and new plants pushed toward a dollar.

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:20.270
That is a procurement price, not a factory receipt.

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:25.130
And it still includes fill finish, quality systems, and thin supplier counts.

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:34.430
People close to high volume inactivated vaccine plants talk about true antigen plus fill costs that can sit well under a dollar a dose.

00:08:35.150 --> 00:08:45.450
Incremental antigen cost in a combination shot is lower still, a drop from the dollar era process into penny scale broth and vial territory once the tanks are full.

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:51.910
Exact cost of goods remains mostly private, so the honest claim is the direction and the magnitude.

00:08:52.910 --> 00:09:01.590
Continuous cell culture and microcarriers remove the monkey bottle neck and collapse the idiot index from many tens towards something much closer to the vial.

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:03.830
The new index is not one.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:12.110
Glass, stoppers, sterile filling, and lot release testing still sit between the magic wand liquid and the box that leaves the plant.

00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:16.070
Those items dominate once the antigen is no longer rare.

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:18.830
Containment is the other remaining tax.

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:31.990
Wild-type seed strains demand high biosafety, which is why Sabin strain IPV, grown from attenuated viruses, is a live first principles attack on factory risk and therefore on cost.

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:41.570
Trade-offs accepted along the way include a product that must be injected, a cold chain, three zero types with type 2 a persistent manufacturing headache,

00:09:41.570 --> 00:09:50.290
and a global supply that proved tight when the World Health Organization asked every country to add at least one IPV dose in the 2010s.

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:53.810
Oral Sabin vaccine is still cheaper to make and to deliver.

00:09:54.410 --> 00:10:01.670
It also sheds and can revert, which is why the eradication endgame cannot live on analogy to the 1960s sugar cube.

00:10:02.130 --> 00:10:06.610
The physical floor of the antigen has been more or less reached at industrial scale.

00:10:06.610 --> 00:10:11.070
The floor of a sterile, documented, globally shipped dose has not.

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:17.290
If the scarce object in your factory is a wild animal's organ, you are not yet making a chemical.

00:10:17.830 --> 00:10:21.130
You are ranching, and ranching does not get cheaper by the decade.

00:10:21.810 --> 00:10:24.450
That is the first portable point from IPV.

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:27.090
The cell substrate is a design choice.

00:10:27.090 --> 00:10:35.750
Banking it, vero, microcarriers, a characterized line is how a biological product is allowed to behave like a manufactured one.

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:44.390
A characterized bank turns a living sheet that dies with the animal into a substrate you can expand, test once, and run like a reactor.

00:10:45.050 --> 00:10:53.630
Until that substitution, every batch reintroduces the lottery of the wild organ, and the factory cannot compound the way a chemical plant compounds.

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:56.670
The second portable point is the kill step.

00:10:57.190 --> 00:11:01.650
A kill step copied as ritual will either fail dangerous or fail expensive.

00:11:02.350 --> 00:11:09.710
Only a mapped kinetic window, formal and time, temperature, no shielded clumps, let safety and cost fall together.

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:15.410
Copy the recipe and you overkill to sleep at night, or you underkill and ship live virus.

00:11:16.170 --> 00:11:20.470
Map the window and the same chemistry that used to be a liturgy becomes a control loop.

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:26.170
Once those two substitutions are done, the vial and the quality system become the product.

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:30.310
Combination shots and multi-dose presentations are not marketing.

00:11:30.870 --> 00:11:37.630
They are the next idiot index fight, because glass, stoppers, sterile filling and lot release now dwarf the antigen.

00:11:38.270 --> 00:11:44.950
Tomorrow the show takes another object apart the same way, historical or living, whoever actually did the reasoning.

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:48.010
The question worth carrying out the door is this.

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:57.170
Which other vaccines still begin with an organ, an egg or a bottle wall, and what is their de-antigen equivalent sitting in a tank that has not been built yet?

